# Wave W17-P (Copperbore Tunnel): bore floor — tidy dug-bore flags: warm tool-brown stone flags laid in sunk joints by the tunnelers’ own hands, with pale tool-mark flecks struck across the tread where the picks dressed them (design: a worked bore, kept tidy — the inspection culture of the Copperbore crews is drawn in the floor’s own art, art layer only; the shipped water, cavecrystal and caveboulder stand byte-preserved beside it). Copperbore’s own floor — split from Comet Falls’ wet grey star-stone by warmth and workmanship (dressed flags, not fallen sky) and from Scorch Path’s ember flags by temperature: this bore is cool, brown, and swept.
